  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency support for earthquake affected populations of Gressier and Gonaives</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This grant is a contribution towards two separate projects implemented by our partner Caritas Switzerland in response to the devastating earthquake of 12 January 2010 in Haiti. In the district of Gressier, located 45 kilometres west of Port-au-Prince in the direction of the epicentre, Caritas Switzerland is working with partners ITECA and the Diocese of Port-au-Prince to provide emergency shelter and kitchen kits to earthquake affected families. Furthermore, Caritas Switzerland will provide schools in Gressier with tents as temporary schooling facilities. In Gonaives, the capital city of the Artibonite region, Caritas Switzerland is working jointly with the Diocesan Education Office which supervises the running of small schools in remote areas. Together they are enabling children who have fled from Port-au-Prince to enrol in school, be supplied with school materials, and be adequately fed.</narrative>
  </description>
